      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "The §3Narrowband Emission Scanning Satellite§r precisely locates specific high-energy events within a 250-meter radius of a target point. It is the high-precision counterpart to the §3Wideband Radio Emission Detector Satellite§r, sensitive to: neutron radiation from nuclear reactors, high-energy particles from fusion reactors and particle accelerators, radar waves from ground radars, and radio waves from §3Satellite Ground Stations§r with an active TX signal.\n\nAll results are stored internally and accessed via §dRedstone-over-Radio§r. \"esurvey\" performs the scan. \"ecount\" writes the result count to RX. \"egetinfo\" followed by an index writes the emission type to RX. \"egetposition\" followed by an index writes the X/Z coordinates - separated by a semicolon - to RX.\n\n§2Events are time-limited. Run repeated scans at short intervals to avoid missing short-lived emissions.",
